// Geometry (verbatim from the paper):
//   Verbatim: free ferromagnet 'Size of FM 15x60x2 (IMA)' nm (Table 2); SOT
//   channel thickness 4 nm; 'the ratio between the length and the width of
//   the ferromagnet must be increased to four in order to maintain a
//   sufficient energy barrier of Eb ~ 40 kT'; thermal barrier Eb = 40 kT; Ms
//   = 1.2e6 A/m; Ku = 0. Transistor count: 'For the SOT-MRAM, since the READ
//   and the WRITE operations are separated, two transistors are needed to
//   avoid sneak currents. The layout area unavoidably increases to 20 F^2 in
//   the case of one WRITE access transistor.' -> 2T1MTJ (1 write + 1 read
//   transistor). Layout in Fig. 1(b) is 4F wide x 5F tall. A 3T1MTJ variant
//   (two write transistors) is 4F x 7F = 28 F^2 and is reported to have
//   worse write EDP.
//
// Provenance: 8 reported, 4 derived, 3 assumed.
// WARNING - these values are NOT from the paper:
//   MemCellLevel = SLC  (no MLC discussion anywhere in paper)
